IMO, they're hard in the early game. They catch up quick though; the first 
tourist I got past both minetown and sokoban ascended.

My advice would be - learn to use your pet(s) and avoid increasing in level 
until you have decent AC, weapon and an escape wand 
(teleport/dig/fire/lightning) or equivalent. Use your camera and use 
Elbereth to keep the monsters off while your pets work. Once you have a 
housecat/dog, you can level up to say level 3, then to say 6 when they go 
large. You must have the equipment to survive independently before XL9, 
unless you can acquire a better pet. Do one or two levels in the mines for 
armour and a mattock (probably your best early weapon) then off to sokoban 
for wands, rings and food before coming back to complete the mines.

If you can't find a mattock, check weapons you find and pick a reasonable 
one to use until you can upgrade to a brand or wish for Grayswandir (I 
assume Grayswandir will blast you BTW).

I was going to ask "why tourists?" but your YAFAP explained that.

